    <!-- SKINMOD: backdrop panel behind the bottom furniture strip (sort/view buttons and the
         A-Z jump letters). See MOD_CHANGELOG 22.

         _t and _h are relative to the Dimension_Furniture_Gutters group, which is 60px tall and
         sits at y950-1010. _x is inset from that group's edges (screen x80 / x1840).

             top  -40  ->  y  910          x inset 60  ->  screen x 140
             + h  130  ->  y 1040                          screen x 1780

         The selectable ink of BOTH strips is y940-1020, centre 980:
           * sort buttons  - the grouplist box is y900-1060, but circlebutton.png carries 40px
             of transparent alpha padding, so the visible pill is only y940-1020.
           * alphabet jump - two rows of 40px letters, y940-1020.
         The panel therefore centres on 975, not on the gutters group's own 980 midpoint, which
         is what made the buttons sit low against the previous y870-1050 slab.

         The faint typed-letter echo above the letters inks y900-930 and now overhangs the top
         by ~10px. To enclose it instead, use -50 / 150.

         _x cannot go much past 60. Button ink width grows 240px per visible button and reaches
         screen x160-1700 at seven (library + Player.HasMedia), so 60 leaves only 20px of
         padding in that worst case and 100 would clip it. See MOD_CHANGELOG 22d. -->
    <constant name="view_furniture_dialog_t">-40</constant>
    <constant name="view_furniture_dialog_h">130</constant>
    <constant name="view_furniture_dialog_x">60</constant>

